<!-- Adaptive-icon foreground layer: the white lotus from the GTK
     app icon (meditate-gtk/.../io.github.janekbt.Meditate.svg).
     The source art lives in a 128-unit space; this layer is the
     108-unit adaptive canvas with a 72-unit safe zone. The outer
     <group> maps source → canvas: scale 0.62 + translate
     (14.32, 11.22) places the lotus bbox centre at ~(54,54) and
     keeps every petal inside the safe zone under any launcher
     mask (group matrix order = translate ∘ scale, pivot 0).
     The petals are white fills with real gaps between them: each
     back petal is cut where a petal in front of it lies, grown by
     1.5 units (outlines computed once and stored as plain points).
     The gaps show whatever is behind the lotus, so it works on the
     blue icon, the accent colours and as the themed icon, which
     reads only the shape. The GTK SVG parts them with a blue
     stroke instead. The base arc is kept (slightly translucent
     white) as in the source. -->
